  },
  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas is in thermodynamic equilibrium. The number of degrees of freedom of a molecule of the gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>. The internal energy of one mole of the gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and the speed of sound in the gas is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math>.&nbsp;At a fixed temperature and pressure, which of the following is the correct option?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>&#60;</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>As we know,&nbsp;internal energy of one mole of the gas&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Clearly,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>n</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is degree of freedom. Therefore, as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;increases,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;also increases.</p><p>Now, speed of sound in gas</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfenced><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><mi>M</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Clearly, as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;increases and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;decreases.</p><p>Hence,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}